# Running without Docker: copy this to `.env`, or just set the variables.
# Nothing here is required for a local trial — the defaults are below.

# The port the server listens on.
PORT=3000

# Where this install is reached from, as the links inside emails should say it. Set this whenever the
# server is behind anything at all (a reverse proxy, a domain name): without it, links are built from
# the Host header of whatever request happened to trigger them — fine on localhost, and wrong
# everywhere else. It is also where Stripe sends the browser back to in multi-tenant mode.
# TICKMARK_PUBLIC_URL=https://tickmark.practice.example

# Where the database lives. The directory is created if it is not there, which makes
# the file the whole backup: copy it and you have copied the practice.
TICKMARK_DATA=data/tickmark.db

# Sending reminders. Optional: with none of these set, Tickmark drafts the message and
# you copy it into whatever you send mail with. `docs/mail.md` is the guide.
#
#   smtp://relay.example:587    STARTTLS when the server offers it (the usual choice)
#   smtps://relay.example:465   TLS from the first byte
#
# Use your existing mail provider as a relay rather than sending directly: a message
# sent straight from a server with no SPF, no DKIM and no reputation lands in spam, and
# no amount of code changes that.
# TICKMARK_SMTP_URL=smtp://user@example.com:your-password@relay.example:587

# The address reminders come from. Has to be one the relay will accept as the sender.
# TICKMARK_MAIL_FROM=Tickmark Practice <office@practice.example>

# How long to wait on the relay before giving up and reporting a failure.
# TICKMARK_SMTP_TIMEOUT_MS=20000

# Only if the relay's certificate comes from your own certificate authority — an
# internal mail server, a corporate relay, one you run yourself. Point this at the CA's
# PEM file and that CA is trusted; without it the machine's normal trust store is used.
# This exists so that trusting your own CA does not require turning verification off.
# TICKMARK_SMTP_CA_FILE=/etc/ssl/my-relay-ca.pem

# Only for a relay on your own machine that offers no encryption at all. With this set,
# a password sent to that relay is readable by anything on the network between here and
# there — which is why it is a separate, deliberate choice and not inferred.
# TICKMARK_SMTP_INSECURE=1

# Texting a reminder. Also optional, and independent of the mail relay: with none of these
# set, reminders go by email as usual. `docs/sms.md` is the guide. The URL is your SMS
# gateway's send endpoint (Twilio's Messages.json and most others take it directly); sign in
# with `user:pass@` in the URL, or a bearer token in TICKMARK_SMS_TOKEN. A text is one line
# and a link — it never carries a document.
# TICKMARK_SMS_URL=https://user:password@api.example.com/2010-04-01/Accounts/abc/Messages.json
# TICKMARK_SMS_FROM=+441234567890
# TICKMARK_SMS_TOKEN=
# TICKMARK_SMS_TIMEOUT_MS=15000

# Multi-tenant (hosted) only. How long a practice keeps its documents after a card fails, in days.
# Stripe chases a failed card for weeks; cutting a working practice off at the first failed charge turns a
# billing hiccup into a cancellation. Set it to 0 to lock out the moment a charge fails. A cancelled
# subscription is never given this slack — that is a decision, not a hiccup.
# TICKMARK_PAST_DUE_GRACE_DAYS=14

# Integration — Xero. Optional: with neither of these set, "Import from Xero" is simply not offered.
# Register a free app at developer.xero.com (OAuth 2.0, a "web app") and put its client id and secret
# here. The redirect URI registered with Xero must match the one used here; it defaults to
# <TICKMARK_PUBLIC_URL>/integrations/xero/callback (so http://localhost works for development — no
# domain needed). Only read scopes are ever requested: this imports a client list and writes nothing
# to anybody's books.
# TICKMARK_XERO_CLIENT_ID=
# TICKMARK_XERO_CLIENT_SECRET=
# TICKMARK_XERO_REDIRECT_URI=

# Integration — QuickBooks. Optional: with neither of these set, "Import from QuickBooks" is not offered.
# Register an app at developer.intuit.com (OAuth 2.0) and put its client id and secret here. The redirect
# URI registered with Intuit must match the one used here; it defaults to
# <TICKMARK_PUBLIC_URL>/integrations/quickbooks/callback. Only read scopes are ever requested.
# TICKMARK_QB_CLIENT_ID=
# TICKMARK_QB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# TICKMARK_QB_REDIRECT_URI=